%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: ec4ba6a512adabf4b8a74985cb2f4d14, type: 3}
  m_Name: DioniseIntroDialogue
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ScriptedDialogue
  nodes:
  - type: 0
    npcLine: New here? Good. I prefer checkpoints where the officer is still paying
      attention.
    animationTrigger: TalkIdle
    cameraTrigger: 
    wobbleText: 0
    choices: []
  - type: 0
    npcLine: Dionise Chkonia. Professor at the university, philosophy and epistemology.
    animationTrigger: TalkIdle
    cameraTrigger: 
    wobbleText: 0
    choices: []
  - type: 0
    npcLine: I've been cross-listing into ethics since the situation escalated. The
      administration finds it useful.
    animationTrigger: TalkIdle
    cameraTrigger: 
    wobbleText: 0
    choices: []
  - type: 1
    npcLine: I'm coming from the archives today. There are texts I want offsite before
      the dust gets worse.
    animationTrigger: TalkLookAway
    cameraTrigger: 
    wobbleText: 0
    choices:
    - playerChoiceText: What kind of texts?
      npcResponse: Primary sources. First editions that exist nowhere else. I'm not
        prepared to let the next one disappear.
      animationTrigger: TalkIdle
    - playerChoiceText: Is the dust getting worse?
      npcResponse: Yes. I don't think the official picture is complete. I stopped
        waiting for full disclosure some time ago.
      animationTrigger: TalkLookDown
  - type: 0
    npcLine: My students are anxious. When everything outside destabilizes, people
      look for structure.
    animationTrigger: TalkIdle
    cameraTrigger: 
    wobbleText: 0
    choices: []
  - type: 0
    npcLine: I keep my lectures on schedule. Routine is its own form of reassurance.
    animationTrigger: TalkIdle
    cameraTrigger: 
    wobbleText: 0
    choices: []
  - type: 1
    npcLine: I have a wife and two children at home. We're managing. Not comfortable,
      but not desperate.
    animationTrigger: TalkLookAway
    cameraTrigger: 
    wobbleText: 0
    choices:
    - playerChoiceText: How are your children holding up?
      npcResponse: Children adapt. What frightens them is watching us pretend we're
        not frightened. So I stopped pretending.
      animationTrigger: TalkLookDown
    - playerChoiceText: You seem very calm about all of this.
      npcResponse: Stoicism. The only rational response to what you cannot control.
        Panic wastes energy where it does least good.
      animationTrigger: TalkIdle
  - type: 0
    npcLine: My papers. I check them every two weeks to avoid delays. The permit
      runs through June.
    animationTrigger: TalkPoint
    cameraTrigger: 
    wobbleText: 0
    choices: []
